From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS: TV systems fill a square screen, sides cropped

NUUBOS_RA_OVERSCAN_X=1 (nuubos-emud: TV systems on a square handheld
screen only): a picture wider than the screen at full height fills the
height as far as at most 8 % of its width (4 % a side) is cropped, and
is scaled to that width beyond; patch 0003 crops the sides evenly. A 4:3
game on the 720x720 RG CubeXX is 783x587 at the top instead of an
integer 2x with large margins (or a 720x540 fit). Not integer scaled.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]

--- a/gfx/video_driver.c
+++ b/gfx/video_driver.c
@@ -2410,6 +2410,24 @@
    return true;
 }
 
+/* nuubOS: NUUBOS_RA_OVERSCAN_X=1 (set by nuubos-emud for TV systems on a
+ * square handheld screen) fills the height with a picture wider than the
+ * screen as far as at most 8 % of its width (4 % a side, within a
+ * TV's overscan) is cropped, scaled to fit beyond that: a 4:3 game on 720x720
+ * is 783x587 at the top, its sides cropped evenly (patch 0003), instead
+ * of a small integer 2x or a 720x540 fit. Not integer: the sharp bilinear
+ * or CRT shader keeps the pixels even. */
+static bool nuubos_overscan_x(void)
+{
+   static int on = -1;
+   if (on < 0)
+   {
+      const char *s = getenv("NUUBOS_RA_OVERSCAN_X");
+      on            = (s && *s == '1') ? 1 : 0;
+   }
+   return on == 1;
+}
+
 /**
  * video_viewport_get_scaled_integer:
  * @vp            : Viewport handle
@@ -2512,7 +2530,20 @@
    /* Make sure that we don't get 0x scale ... */
    else if (width >= content_width && height >= content_height)
    {
-      if (keep_aspect)
+      unsigned nuubos_w = (unsigned)roundf(height * aspect_ratio);
+
+      if (keep_aspect && nuubos_overscan_x() && nuubos_w > width)
+      {
+         unsigned nuubos_h = height;
+         if (nuubos_w * 0.92f > width)
+         {
+            nuubos_w = (unsigned)roundf(width / 0.92f);
+            nuubos_h = (unsigned)roundf(nuubos_w / aspect_ratio);
+         }
+         padding_x = (int)width  - (int)nuubos_w;
+         padding_y = (int)height - (int)nuubos_h;
+      }
+      else if (keep_aspect)
       {
          int8_t half_w       = 0;
          int8_t half_h       = 0;
